From 9fbb8e9e960bd9dc43ec9a57e5de5357366e986f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nau Fantom <353563530+nauxph@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:10:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] perf: copy occlusion results after one barrier on AMD,
 not a wait per query

SamplesStreamer::PresyncWrites copied each bank's occlusion results with
VK_QUERY_RESULT_WAIT_BIT. AMD's Windows driver spends about 22 us per
query on that wait, and Ocarina of Time resolves about 2,000 queries a
frame: 45 ms of a 61 ms GPU frame at the Kokiri village sign (RX 9070 XT,
driver 2.0.395, GPU Fast, docked 1440p).

On AMD drivers, one ALL_COMMANDS -> TRANSFER barrier before the copies now
orders them after every earlier command, including the vkCmdEndQuery that
made each query available, and the copies run without the wait: 0.4 ms a
frame. Other drivers were not measured and keep the wait.

Same scene and session, three 600-frame windows each, no frame trace:
            before   after
  fps        19.7     34.7
  p50 ms     50.5     28.7
  p95 ms     55.9     34.2
  p99 ms     66.0     42.0
  1% low     15.2     23.9 fps
No flashes, missing objects or flicker while switching live, and the
screenshots match. With EDEN_DKB_FRAME_TRACE=1, a DKB query_copies line
logs the copies per second.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
