From f02c9ca37d4e333ec4656d85c2ca4aaf5bd4c9de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nau Fantom <353563530+nauxph@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:50:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] vk_pipeline_cache: keep Switch 2 pipelines up to a memory
 budget

Port of Lichii PR 313 by madebyjordan (head 09d20d291a), the reviewed
form of Eglantine PR 696.

Ocarina of Time destroyed every pipeline unused for 9000 frames
(~2.5 min), so going back to an area or meeting the same enemies again
rebuilt them in bursts. A 78-minute session on an RX 9070 XT evicted and
rebuilt about 10,000 pipelines and held draws for 168 s. The AMD
driver's cache missed many of the rebuilds: one pipeline took 111-131 ms
on each of its five builds.

Switch 2 titles now keep their pipelines up to 1/8 of system RAM at
~0.45 MB each (about 9,300 with 32 GB). Past that, the least recently
used are evicted, and still only ones unused for 9000 frames: evicting
pipelines used moments before lost the device on AMD. A pipeline that
fails to build at boot is left out of the cache, so the first draw that
needs it builds it again. Switch 1 titles keep the 9000-frame rule.

Co-authored-by: Jordan <madebyjordan@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-authored-by: monsterlag <64719697+monsterlag@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
