From 637630ab2fffc8b1b726220153ff83992409bc8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nau Fantom <353563530+nauxph@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:46:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] vulkan: skip heavy unbuilt pipelines by default, also
 without async shaders

The heavy skip needed EDEN_NX2_HEAVY_SKIP and asynchronous shaders. In
Ocarina of Time on an RX 9070 XT it cut draws held per new pipeline from
111-124 ms to 20 ms, frames over 100 ms from 5.6-13.4 to 2.9 a minute
and the worst frame from 7-11 s to 2.4 s (an area load), with no missing
objects seen. It now runs by default and ahead of the asynchronous
shaders check, with the same guards.

- ParseHeavySkipWords: unset or "1" keep 4000 instructions, "0", "off",
  "false" or "no" turn it off, and a number sets the threshold.
  DecideHeavyPending makes the decision. Both have [heavy_skip] tests.
- A draw the guards keep still waits, or with asynchronous shaders goes
  to the native_async_draws setting (Bounded, Skip) instead of waiting
  for the whole build.
- Only native draws track render targets and clears, so titles without
  native pipelines do no extra work.
- A draw skipped on purpose no longer logs "Draw skipped (no pipeline)".
  The 10 s heavy_skip report only appears when a heavy draw was judged,
  and the boot log states the threshold.
- The held-draw log copies the hold details when the draw is recorded,
  so a later draw of the same pipeline cannot change them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
